<LegalLayout title="Payment Policy" description="How publishing package fees, NDA fees and printing costs are invoiced, split and paid at Chance Publishers." updated="18 August 2026">
  <h2>How publishing fees are structured</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>NDA processing fee</strong> — a fixed fee (currently KSh 1,000) payable when you start your project, before your manuscript can be reviewed.</li>
    <li><strong>Publishing package fee</strong> (Bronze, Silver or Gold) — payable in two parts: a <strong>70% deposit</strong>, invoiced and payable at the same time as your NDA fee to secure your project's start, and a <strong>30% balance</strong>, due before your final, print-ready files are released to you.</li>
    <li><strong>Printing costs</strong> — quoted and invoiced separately once your final page count, paper, binding and quantity are confirmed, since these depend on your finished book.</li>
    <li><strong>Launch and other add-on services</strong> — quoted separately if requested.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How to pay</h2>
  <p>We currently accept:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Bank transfer</strong> — transfer to the account details provided by our team, then upload your proof of payment through the portal.</li>
    <li><strong>M-Pesa</strong> — where enabled, pay directly from the invoice page in your author portal via an M-Pesa STK push prompt to your phone.</li>
    <li><strong>Cash or cheque</strong> — accepted in person at our office, recorded and verified by our finance team.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How payments are verified</h2>
  <p>Every payment is verified before an invoice is marked as paid:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Bank transfer proof is checked against our account statement by our finance team.</li>
    <li>M-Pesa payments are confirmed automatically once Safaricom sends a successful payment notification for the exact transaction.</li>
    <li>Cash and cheque payments are recorded by an administrator at the point of receipt, and cheques are cleared before being marked verified.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>A payment that has not yet been verified will show as "pending" in your portal — this is normal and simply means our team hasn't confirmed it yet.</p>

  <h2>Receipts and invoices</h2>
  <p>An official receipt is generated and made available to you in the author portal for every verified payment. All invoices and receipts remain accessible in your portal for your records.</p>

  <h2>Order of work</h2>
  <p>Editorial and design work on each stage of your book begins once the payment for that stage has been verified. Working on staged, verified payments protects both you and us — you are never asked to pay in full for services not yet delivered, and we are able to commit staff and freelancer time to your project with confidence.</p>

  <h2>Late or outstanding balances</h2>
  <p>If your 30% balance remains outstanding, your final, print-ready files will not be released until it is paid. This does not affect your ownership of your manuscript — see our <a href="/legal/copyright-ownership">Copyright &amp; Manuscript Ownership</a> policy.</p>
</LegalLayout>
